      "content": "The central debate surrounding economic sanctions is a longstanding one, with proponents arguing that they are a crucial tool for promoting democracy and holding authoritarian regimes accountable, while critics contend that they are a blunt instrument wielded by powerful nations to exert control over weaker ones. In reality, sanctions have consistently proven to be a double-edged sword, often backfiring and strengthening the very regimes they aim to topple. By examining the historical record, it becomes clear that sanctions are a tool of the powerful, used to maintain their influence and suppress dissent, rather than a genuine means of promoting democracy.",
